  "about": [
    "Shared test vectors of the pairing URI (version 1) that the HUD shows as a QR code and the companion app scans.",
    "valid: `uri` parses to `payload`; where `canonical`, encoding `payload` gives exactly `uri`. hudName null: no `n` parameter.",
    "invalid: parsing `uri` fails with `error`: 'foreign' (not a carheadsup pairing URI), 'unsupported-version' (a later version: update the app) or 'invalid'.",
    "Asserted by packages/core/test/protocol/pairing.test.ts and companion-android/protocol (PairingUriTest; ContractSyncTest checks its copy",
    "against this file). Never change a vector: add one. (When pairing tokens became printable ASCII without spaces, the one vector whose token broke that rule moved to `invalid` under a new name, its URI unchanged.)"
